Yang Cui received her B.S. under the supervision of Prof. Yonghong Cao in 2018 from Northeast Normal University. Currently, she is studying for a Ph.D. in Prof. Hongwei Hou's group at Zhengzhou University. Her research interests mainly focus on the development and performance exploration of functional MOFs and the composites.
Yujie Zhao received her B.S. in 2016, and she is studying for a Ph.D. at Zhengzhou University in Prof. Hongwei Hou's group. Her research interests are the application of MOF composites in the field of photocatalysis.
Jie Wu received his Ph.D. in 2007 from Zhengzhou University under the supervision of Prof. Hongwei Hou From 2009 to 2012, he was a postdoctoral research associate in Prof. Junbiao Chang's group at Zhengzhou University. From 2017 to 2018, he was a visiting scholar in Omar Farha group at Northwestern University in USA. His research interests focus on the development of porous MOFs for heterogeneously catalytic applications.
Hongwei Hou received his Ph.D. from Nanjing University in 1995. After post-doctoral research at Hong Kong University of Science and Technology and the National University of Singapore from 1995 to 1998, he returned to China to take his current position. His research interests focus on the crystalline post-synthesis modification, the nonlinear optical properties, the construction and development of MOFs and the composites.
